{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>He gave</b> — And he did not mention \"the thing\" and \"the hail,\" because Pharaoh did not ask Moses to remove the plague." "<b>And fire of flames</b> — Corresponding to ותהלך אש ארצה (\"and fire walked through the land\"). And it lacks a bet [in להבות]. [Either] אש בלהבות, or אש is an attributive noun — sometimes אש, sometimes אש להבות — in the manner of חרבות צורים (\"flints of rock\"), [where in the parallel one reads] אף תשיב צור חרבו (\"even rock its sword\")."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 105, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:33.087481311Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}